Use loopback multicast for a local pairing test; a builder's LAN firewall
must not determine whether its two local peers can discover one another.
The multicast transport and authenticated pairing remain exercised.

Own both new-pairing clients, observe either application peer's failure
without first waiting for the listener, and bound exchange and cancellation.
The old five-second timeout did not cover the preceding listener wait;
a failed peer could leave that wait blocked until the 300-second watchdog.
Use loopback for this local pairing too, retaining TLS and encrypted packets.

